{
  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "Contradictory central testing methods: Table 8-1 says local KRAS G12C results available uses Study 20190009, but text says confirmation can occur through Study 20190294",
      "page": 97,
      "quote": "This central laboratory testing can occur through the current protocol or Amgen Study 20190294. ... Local KRAS G12C results available Archived tissue through the Study 20190009 protocol",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent tissue collection window: page 97 says no time limit, page 98 says within 5 years",
      "page": 98,
      "quote": "collected within 5 years",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Multiple testing procedure description contradicts itself: text says ORR tested at α/5 (0.005) after PFS rejection, but figure legend and later text imply different alpha propagation",
      "page": 101,
      "quote": "if the hypothesis of PFS is rejected, ORR will be tested using 1-sided α/5 (0.005) level. With the rejection of ORR hypothesis, OS will be tested using 1-sided full α (0.025) level. If ORR hypothesis is failed to be rejected, OS will be tested using 1-sided 0.001 level if at PFS IA, otherwise using 4α/5 (0.02) level.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Interim analysis timing inconsistent: text says 70% (160 events) but Table 9-1 says 70% and 160 events, yet also says 'or LSE + 6 weeks' which is not a percentage",
      "page": 107,
      "quote": "An IA of PFS for superiority is planned when approximately 70% (160 events) of the total PFS events have been observed, or when the enrollment is finished and the last randomized subject have had the opportunity to have 6 weeks of follow up, whichever occurs later.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "OS at PFS PA timing inconsistent: text says 'after 175 OS events (~53% maturity)' but Table 9-1 says 175 OS events at 19 months, and OS PA says 198 events at 22 months",
      "page": 107,
      "quote": "the OS will be assessed for superiority of AMG 510 over docetaxel at either the time of PFS primary analysis or after 175 OS events (~53% maturity) have been observed, whichever is later.",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Primary analysis of PFS: text says 230 PFS events, but Table 9-1 says 230 PFS events at 100% information fraction, yet text says 'approximately 230' and '100%' is inconsistent with 160 being 70% (160/0.7=228.6, so 230 is ~100%)",
      "page": 108,
      "quote": "The timing for the PA of PFS will be event driven and will happen when approximately 230 PFS events are reached cumulatively in 2 treatment groups.",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Covariates list includes race twice: once as stratification factor and once as additional covariate",
      "page": 105,
      "quote": "In addition to the stratification factors for randomization, number of prior lines of therapy in advanced disease (1 versus 2 versus > 2), race (Asian versus non-Asian), history of CNS involvement (yes versus no), the following additional covariates may be included: ... race",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Subgroups list includes race as a subgroup but also as a stratification factor, and includes STK11/KEAP1 mutations without specifying categories",
      "page": 106,
      "quote": "race (white, black, Asian, other) ... STK11 mutation ... KEAP1 mutation",
      "severity": "minor"
    },
    {
      "title": "Missing information: No sample size or randomization ratio provided in the statistical section",
      "page": 100,
      "quote": "9. Statistical Considerations",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Endpoint analysis mismatch: H04-H08 are key secondary endpoints but the multiple testing procedure only describes testing PFS, OS, ORR, then 3 symptoms, then 2 PROs, but there are 5 PRO endpoints (dyspnea, cough, chest pain, physical functioning, global health status) and the text says 'next 3 endpoints' and 'next 2 PRO endpoints'",
      "page": 102,
      "quote": "If all 3 hypotheses of PFS, OS, ORR are rejected, the next 3 endpoints of change from baseline over time to week 12 in 3 lung cancer symptoms will be tested using Holm’s procedure",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Inconsistent analysis method for PRO endpoints: Section 9.4.2.1 says MMRM for dyspnea, physical functioning, global health status, but GEE for cough and chest pain; however, the hypotheses list all five as key secondary endpoints and the multiple testing procedure treats them in two groups, but the text says 'all 6 hypotheses' when there are only 5 PRO hypotheses (H04-H08) plus PFS, OS, ORR makes 8 total",
      "page": 102,
      "quote": "If all 6 hypotheses listed above are rejected, the next 2 PRO endpoints will be tested",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "title": "Missing cross-reference: Section 4.4 is referenced for end of study definition but not provided in excerpt",
      "page": 107,
      "quote": "the final analysis will be conducted and reported following the end of study, as defined in Section 4.4.",
      "severity": "minor"
    }
  ]
}
